## Project facts
- Base URL: `https://api.superlinked.com`. OpenAI-compatible base: `https://api.superlinked.com/v1`.
- API key lives in the `SIE_API_KEY` environment variable on the server only. Never send it to the browser and never commit it.
- Primary scoring: `POST /v1/decisions` (OpenAI Decisions format) with predicate, choice and score questions batched in ONE request per transcript window. Model example from the docs: `fastino/GLiNER2.5-Decide`. Confirm it is available on Serverless in the model catalog.
- Answers come back in question order. Map by index and assert the length. Predicate answers carry `probability`; choice answers carry `choice`; score answers carry `score`.
- Input is text only and must fit the model window. Oversized input returns 400 and is never truncated. Keep windows to the last 6 caller utterances (about 1,500 characters).
- TypeScript SDK for encode, score and extract: `@superlinked/sie-sdk`. For decisions, use the `openai` package with the SIE base URL if it exposes `decisions`, otherwise plain `fetch` with the same JSON body.

## Live-path rules (the demo must never hang)
- The SDK default is to wait for cold capacity for up to 900 seconds. The live scoring client must NOT do that. Disable waiting (`waitForCapacity: false`) or set a short `provisionTimeout` (about 1500 ms). On `ProvisioningError`, 503 `PROVISIONING`, 429 or timeout, fall back to the keyword scorer immediately and show `scorer: keyword`.
- Use a separate warm-up client with waiting enabled.
- Do not set `remote: "forbid"` on the live client. Relay answering during a cold start is a safety net.
- Warm means served by dedicated capacity: response header `X-SIE-Served-By: local` (SDK: `result.request.servedBy === "local"`). `remote` with `X-SIE-Upstream: sie-relay` means it was relayed. Show this on the dashboard footer.
- Dedicated capacity starts when sustained demand warrants it, so a single ping may not warm a model. Warm-up: starting about 20 minutes before a demo, send a light sustained loop (about 1 request per 2 seconds per model) until three consecutive responses report `local`, then drop to 1 per minute.

## Rate limits (Serverless, per key)
- Realtime endpoints (`/v1/encode`, `/v1/score`, `/v1/extract`, `/v1/embeddings`): 50 requests/s, 32 in flight.
- Generation endpoints: 5 requests/s, 4 in flight.
- `/v1/decisions` is not listed in that table. Confirm which limit applies.
- A 429 carries `Retry-After` and `X-SIE-Error-Code: RATE_LIMIT`. Refused requests are not billed.
- Our rules: at most one scoring request per 700 ms, at most 2 in flight, never run `scripts/bench.ts` against the live key during a demo.

## Style
- Wrap SIE access in one module (`gatekeeper/lib/server/risk.ts`) behind a small interface so the scorer can be swapped to the keyword fallback.
- Log request id, status, latency and `servedBy` for every call.
